# Flags every build in this project uses, whatever the target.
#
# Include this from any hxml. Keeping them in one file rather than repeating them per build is
# not tidiness — a flag that changes generated code has to be on *every* path that produces it,
# or the thing measured and the thing shipped stop being the same program.

# Haxe's optimising analyzer: constant and copy propagation, local dead-code elimination,
# expression fusion. Verified behaviour-preserving here — every conformance digest is identical
# with it on both targets — which is the only evidence that counts for a project whose promise is
# bit-identical output. It also gives an immature C++ generator a smaller typed AST to chew on.
-D analyzer-optimize
